<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/" xmlns:lex="https://lexipedia.xyz/ns/lex/1.0" id="dmn_permit_required" name="Building permit required? Small residential projects in Virginia, DC and North Carolina" namespace="https://lexipedia.xyz/ns/decision/permit_required" exporter="lexflow (design prototype)" exporterVersion="0.1">
  <description>Whether a building permit is required for a shed, playhouse, deck, fence, wall, retaining wall, addition, play equipment, storage container or farm building at a detached one- or two-family dwelling or townhouse, and for wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it, from state-adopted text only: 13VAC5-63 (USBC Part I), 12-A DCMR 105, 10-C DCMR 303 and 304, and N.C. Gen. Stat. 160D-1110 and 143-138, as held in the lexflow regulations and statutes indexes (open-us-law v2026.09.1, snapshot 2026-09-30). No model-code text. Every rule quotes the words it rests on. Draft for review, not legal advice.</description>
  <extensionElements>
    <lex:model id="permit_required" jurisdictions="va dc nc" reviewStatus="draft" method="assistant-edited" corpora="regulations statutes" snapshot="open-us-law v2026.09.1 (2026-09-30)" design="docs/design/permit-required.md">
      <lex:consumer place="City of Charlottesville" govId="47210400100000" process="building_permit" fixture="fixtures/places/va/discovery-charlottesville.json" jurisdiction="va"/>
      <lex:consumer place="Albemarle County" govId="47100200200000" process="building_permit_residential" fixture="fixtures/places/va/discovery-albemarle.json" jurisdiction="va"/>
      <lex:consumer place="City of Staunton" govId="47213000100000" process="residential_building_permit" fixture="fixtures/places/va/discovery-staunton.json" jurisdiction="va"/>
    </lex:model>
  </extensionElements>
  <inputData id="in_jurisdiction" name="jurisdiction" label="Jurisdiction (state or District)">
    <description>The state-level rule set: "va" (Virginia USBC, statewide, enforced by the city, county or town building department), "dc" (District of Columbia Construction Codes), "nc" (North Carolina statutes only). A Virginia locality cannot change the exemption list (13VAC5-63-20 B; Va. Code § 36-98). In North Carolina a local variance cannot require a permit that the $40,000 exclusion removes (G.S. 143-138(b5)), but a county or city may adopt floodplain management regulations and, once the Code Council approves them, fire prevention code provisions (143-138(e)); and inside fire limits (which a county may, and a city must, establish under 160D-1128) a frame or wooden building or addition needs the inspection department's permit. See docs/design/permit-required.md part 5. Allowed values: "va", "dc", "nc".</description>
    <variable id="in_jurisdiction_var" name="jurisdiction" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_project" name="project" label="Project">
    <description>What is built, at a detached one- or two-family dwelling or a townhouse (the model's scope). "shed": a tool or storage shed (a garden storage shed in DC). "playhouse": a playhouse or tree house. "deck": a new deck, or new deck framing. "deck_resurfacing": replacing the decking, railings, pickets or stair treads of an existing deck, framing unchanged. "fence": a new fence, or the replacement of an existing fence, in kind or not. "fence_repair": repair in kind of an existing fence (DC item 4 exempts "Repair in kind" only). "masonry_wall": a freestanding concrete or masonry wall (not retaining soil). "retaining_wall": a wall that retains soil. "addition": an addition to the dwelling (a room, a porch with a roof, an attached garage). "playground_equipment": swing sets, slides, climbing bars, jungle gyms, skateboard ramps and similar play equipment (VA 102.3 item 7, DC 105.2 Building item 12); a play structure that is a small building is a playhouse. "storage_container": an off-site manufactured intermodal freight, moving or storage container placed on the lot, temporarily or permanently, for use as a storage container (VA 102.3 item 11); one fitted out for another use is not. "farm_building": a farm building or structure as 13VAC5-63-200 and Va. Code § 36-97 define it (not used for residential purposes, on property where farming operations take place, used primarily for farm uses), no part of it operated as a restaurant. An industrialized (modular) building takes the answer for what it is (a shed, an addition): 102.3 item 8 exempts it from the USBC except Section 429, and 429.5 applies the code's permit requirements to its site work. Other repairs, pools and signs are outside the model; wiring, plumbing, gas and mechanical work is the input trade_work. Allowed values: "shed", "playhouse", "deck", "deck_resurfacing", "fence", "fence_repair", "masonry_wall", "retaining_wall", "addition", "playground_equipment", "storage_container", "farm_building".</description>
    <variable id="in_project_var" name="project" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_floor_area_sqft" name="floor_area_sqft" label="Floor or building area (sq ft)">
    <description>Sheds and playhouses: the building area (VA 108.2 item 2) or area (DC 105.2 items 8 and 13), in square feet.</description>
    <variable id="in_floor_area_sqft_var" name="floor_area_sqft" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_one_story" name="one_story" label="One story">
    <description>Sheds and playhouses in VA: the structure has one story (item 2).</description>
    <variable id="in_one_story_var" name="one_story" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_attached_to_dwelling" name="attached_to_dwelling" label="Attached to the dwelling">
    <description>Sheds and playhouses in VA: item 2 covers only detached structures. An attached shed is construction of, or an addition to, a building. No VA, DC or NC deck rule on disk turns on attachment.</description>
    <variable id="in_attached_to_dwelling_var" name="attached_to_dwelling" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_group_f1_or_h" name="group_f1_or_h" label="Classified as Group F-1 or H">
    <description>VA sheds and playhouses: true when the building official classifies the structure as a Group F-1 (factory) or H (hazardous) occupancy, which item 2 excludes. A shed that stores ordinary household tools is neither.</description>
    <variable id="in_group_f1_or_h_var" name="group_f1_or_h" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_height_ft" name="height_ft" label="Height (ft)">
    <description>Measured as the applicable text measures it: a VA concrete or masonry wall above the finished grade, not counting ornamental column caps (item 6); a DC shed's overall height (item 8); a DC retaining wall from the bottom of the footing to the top of the wall (item 10). No deck rule on disk uses height above grade.</description>
    <variable id="in_height_ft_var" name="height_ft" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_unbalanced_fill_ft" name="unbalanced_fill_ft" label="Unbalanced fill supported (ft)">
    <description>VA retaining walls: the depth of unbalanced fill the wall supports (item 7).</description>
    <variable id="in_unbalanced_fill_ft_var" name="unbalanced_fill_ft" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_surcharge_or_liquids" name="surcharge_or_liquids" label="Retaining wall supports a surcharge or impounds liquids">
    <description>VA retaining walls: true when the wall supports a surcharge other than ordinary unbalanced fill (for example a driveway, parking or a building above it) or is built to impound Class I, II or III-A liquids (item 7).</description>
    <variable id="in_surcharge_or_liquids_var" name="surcharge_or_liquids" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_land_disturbance_sqft" name="land_disturbance_sqft" label="Area of land disturbance (sq ft)">
    <description>DC retaining walls: the area of land disturbed by the work (105.2 item 10).</description>
    <variable id="in_land_disturbance_sqft_var" name="land_disturbance_sqft" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_other_exempt_shed_on_lot" name="other_exempt_shed_on_lot" label="Another exempted storage shed is already on the lot">
    <description>DC sheds: item 8 exempts a single shed on a lot with no other exempted storage shed.</description>
    <variable id="in_other_exempt_shed_on_lot_var" name="other_exempt_shed_on_lot" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_safety_barrier" name="safety_barrier" label="Fence is a pool barrier or required for pedestrian safety">
    <description>VA fences: true when the fence is the barrier for a swimming pool, or is required for pedestrian safety under Section 3306 (protection of pedestrians during construction) (item 5).</description>
    <variable id="in_safety_barrier_var" name="safety_barrier" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_cost_usd" name="cost_usd" label="Cost of the work (USD)">
    <description>NC: the cost of the work, for the $40,000 exclusion of G.S. 160D-1110(c) and 143-138(b5).</description>
    <variable id="in_cost_usd_var" name="cost_usd" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_historic" name="historic" label="In a historic district or historically designated">
    <description>The property is in a historic district (VA: one created by the locality under Va. Code § 15.2-2306; NC: a designated district or landmark under Part 4 of Article 9 of Chapter 160D), or the building or structure is historically designated (DC 105.2.5). Ask whenever the question does not say: it changes the DC answer.</description>
    <variable id="in_historic_var" name="historic" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_flood_hazard_area" name="flood_hazard_area" label="In a (special) flood hazard area">
    <description>The work is in a special flood hazard area (VA Exception 2; for a VA farm building, the 'flood plain' of 102.3 item 9) or on premises wholly or partially within a Flood Hazard Area (DC 105.2.6).</description>
    <variable id="in_flood_hazard_area_var" name="flood_hazard_area" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_trade_work" name="trade_work" label="Includes wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work">
    <description>Every project: true when the work includes installing, extending or altering electric wiring, plumbing (water supply, drainage or vent piping), gas or other fuel piping, or heating, cooling or other mechanical systems, for example a circuit, outlet or light run to a shed or deck, a water line or drain, or a gas line to a grill. False for the minor and like-for-like work the state lists exempt: low-voltage, broadband, utility or monitoring wiring (VA 108.2 item 1), like-for-like replacement of fixtures, switches, receptacles, lighting fixtures, appliances or LP-gas containers (VA 108.2 items 10 and 14.2 to 14.4; the Electrical, Gas, Mechanical and Plumbing lists of DC 105.2; NC 160D-1110(a)(2) and (4)).</description>
    <variable id="in_trade_work_var" name="trade_work" typeRef="boolean"/>
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="in_dwelling" name="dwelling" label="Kind of dwelling">
    <description>NC deck resurfacing: the dwelling the work is at. The $40,000 exclusion of G.S. 160D-1110(c) and 143-138(b5) reaches only a "single-family residence" (or a farm or commercial building): "two_family" is outside it, and whether a "townhouse" unit is a single-family residence the statutes do not say. Not asked elsewhere. Allowed values: "single_family", "two_family", "townhouse".</description>
    <variable id="in_dwelling_var" name="dwelling" typeRef="string"/>
  </inputData>
