  <knowledgeSource id="ks_dc303" name="10-C DCMR 303 (Historic preservation: permit requirements, general)" locationURI="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile=3092545F-0000-C45F-90B0-FDCCA7A2E4C6">
    <description>303.1 and 303.3: work on historic properties needs a permit, but the construction permit is governed by 12 DCMR Chapter 1 and no separate preservation permit is required.</description>
    <extensionElements>
      <lex:reference citation="10-C DCMR 303" state="dc" corpus="regulations" kind="regulation" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T10_C_C10_C3_S303" indexTitle="PERMIT REQUIREMENTS: GENERAL"/>
    </extensionElements>
    <type>regulation</type>
  </knowledgeSource>
  <decision id="d_permit_required" name="permit_required" label="Is a building permit required?">
    <description>permit: yes (a permit, or a permit application, is required), no (no permit is required), or depends. The officials' discretion is treated one way throughout: the answer is yes where the text requires a permit unless the building official deems the work exempt (VA 108.2 items 13 and 14.11), with that caveat in the basis; it is depends where the text exempts the work but lets an official require a permit anyway (VA Exception 2), or where the answer turns on a question the text on disk does not settle (whether work is a DC 'ordinary repair', whether a playhouse is an 'other site feature', what the North Carolina code books require for work the statute does not take out of its $40,000 exclusion). Where the statute does take NC work out of the exclusion (new load-bearing structure, over $40,000, a two-family dwelling, trade work), the answer is yes on the reading that the Code requires the permit, and it would change if the code books exempt the work. exemption: the exemption item that applies or was displaced, or none. One UNIQUE table: precedence (105.2.5 and 105.2.6 over 105.2; Exception 2 over 108.2; trade work over the structure's exemption) is spelled out row by row, never by rule order.</description>
    <question>Does this project need a building permit under the state (or District) text, and which exemption item applies?</question>
    <variable id="d_permit_required_var" name="permit_required"/>
