          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in14">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_out0">
          <text>"depends"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_out1">
          <text>"12-A DCMR 105.2.2 (ordinary repairs)"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r33_out2">
          <text>"It may be an ordinary repair, which needs no permit, but not if it removes or cuts a structural beam or load-bearing support. Ask the code official. This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2.2 (reading): “Permits are not required for ordinary repairs to buildings, other structures or equipment.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r34">
        <description>DC: new fence, or replacing an existing fence</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 4" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/4" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Repair in kind of existing fences.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1.1, item 7.4" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1.1/7.4" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>7.4 Fences.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Unless specifically exempted under Section 105.2, an owner or authorized agent who intends to undertake any of the activities set forth in items 1 through 5 below, or to cause any such work to be done shall first make application to the code official and obtain the required permit(s) relevant to the intended work</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 7" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/7" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="implied" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Replacement in kind of one of the items listed hereafter.</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: item 7 exempts replacement in kind only of the items it lists (7.1 to 7.7), and fences are not among them, so item 4's 'Repair in kind' does not reach a replacement; 105.2.5's paraphrase of item 4 points the other way.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in0">
          <text>"dc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in1">
          <text>"fence"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_out1">
          <text>"none"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r34_out2">
          <text>"Item 4 exempts only repair in kind of an existing fence, and 105.1.1 classes fence permits among the miscellaneous permits. Replacing an existing fence, even in kind, is answered here as a new fence (a judgement call): item 7's replacement-in-kind list has no fences. 105.2.5 describes item 4 as 'Repair or replacement of fences', so ask the code official whether a replacement in kind is treated as exempt."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 4; 12-A DCMR 105.1.1, item 7.4; 12-A DCMR 105.1; 12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 7 (reading): “Repair in kind of existing fences.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r35">
        <description>DC: repair in kind of an existing fence (not a replacement), not historic, not in a Flood Hazard Area</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 4" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/4" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Repair in kind of existing fences.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>This Section 105.2 sets forth exemptions from permit requirements, subject to historic and Flood Hazard Area restrictions set forth in Sections 105.2.5 and 105.2.6 respectively.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r35_in0">
