        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r40_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r40_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r40_out0">
          <text>"no"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r40_out1">
          <text>"12-A DCMR 105.2 Building item 10"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r40_out2">
          <text>"Exempt: a retaining wall no more than four feet high (from the bottom of the footing) disturbing 50 sq ft of land or less. This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 10; 12-A DCMR 105.2: “Retaining walls that are not over four feet (1219 mm) in height, measured from the bottom of the footing to the top of the wall, only where the area of land disturbance does not exceed 50 square feet (4.65 m2).”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r41">
        <description>DC: an item-10 retaining wall in a historic district</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2.5" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2.5" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>and the work is to occur on the land of or the exterior of buildings or other structures located in historic districts, or of historically designated buildings or other structures, an application for a building permit subject only to historic preservation review pursuant to Section 105.1 shall be required for the following work described in Section 105.2 Building</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2.5" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2.5" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>and 10. Retaining walls</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2.5" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2.5" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>The code official shall not issue a permit based on an application subject solely to historic preservation review under this section without the prior review and approval of the Historic Preservation Office.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="10-C DCMR 304.2" section="10-C DCMR 304" subsection="304.2" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile=3092545F-0000-C379-A514-3E614E04143B" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T10_C_C10_C3_S304">
              <lex:quote>a permit is required for various minor repairs to historic landmarks or properties within historic districts, even though a permit is not required for the same work on non-historic properties</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="10-C DCMR 304.2(e)" section="10-C DCMR 304" subsection="304.2/e" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile=3092545F-0000-C379-A514-3E614E04143B" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T10_C_C10_C3_S304">
              <lex:quote>Replacement of retaining walls regardless of height</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in0">
          <text>"dc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in1">
          <text>"retaining_wall"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in6">
          <text>&lt;= 4</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in9">
          <text>&lt;= 50</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in13">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in14">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_out1">
          <text>"12-A DCMR 105.2 item 10, not available under 105.2.5"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r41_out2">
          <text>"In a historic district a building permit application subject only to historic preservation review is required. 10-C DCMR 304.2(e) agrees: replacing a retaining wall of any height there needs a permit."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2.5; 10-C DCMR 304.2; 10-C DCMR 304.2(e): “and the work is to occur on the land of or the exterior of buildings or other structures located in historic districts, or of historically designated buildings or other structures, an application for a building permit subject only to historic preservation review pursuant to Section 105.1 shall be required for the following work described in Section 105.2 Building”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r42">
