        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r47_out2">
          <text>"New deck framing adds load-bearing structure, so the $40,000 exclusion does not apply; 160D-1110(a) requires the permits the State Building Code requires."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(1) (reading); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(1); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a) (reading): “The addition, repair, or replacement of load-bearing structures.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r48">
        <description>NC: replacing the decking, pickets, railings or stair treads, $40,000 or less, single-family residence</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(1)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c/1" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>However, no permit is required for replacement of windows, doors, exterior siding, or the pickets, railings, stair treads, and decking of porches and exterior decks that otherwise meet the requirements of this subsection.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>No permit issued under Article 9 of Chapter 143 of the General Statutes is required for any construction, installation, repair, replacement, or alteration costing forty thousand dollars ($40,000) or less and performed in accordance with the current edition of the North Carolina State Building Code in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building unless the work involves any of the following</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b5)" section="143-138" subsection="b5" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_143/GS_143-138.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C143_S143-138">
              <lex:quote>No permit shall be required under the Code or any local variance thereof approved under subsection (e) for any construction, installation, repair, replacement, or alteration performed in accordance with the current edition of the North Carolina State Building Code and costing forty thousand dollars ($40,000) or less in any single family residence, farm building, or commercial building</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in1">
          <text>"deck_resurfacing"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in12">
          <text>&lt;= 40000</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_in16">
          <text>"single_family"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_out0">
          <text>"no"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_out1">
          <text>"G.S. 160D-1110(c)(1)"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r48_out2">
          <text>"No permit: replacing the decking, pickets, railings or stair treads of an existing deck of a single-family residence, at $40,000 or less, done to the State Building Code. A local variance cannot require one (143-138(b5)). This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(1); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b5): “However, no permit is required for replacement of windows, doors, exterior siding, or the pickets, railings, stair treads, and decking of porches and exterior decks that otherwise meet the requirements of this subsection.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r49">
        <description>NC: replacing the decking, pickets, railings or stair treads, over $40,000</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>No permit issued under Article 9 of Chapter 143 of the General Statutes is required for any construction, installation, repair, replacement, or alteration costing forty thousand dollars ($40,000) or less and performed in accordance with the current edition of the North Carolina State Building Code in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building unless the work involves any of the following</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(1)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a/1" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The construction, reconstruction, alteration, repair, movement to another site, removal, or demolition of any building or structure.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>no person shall commence or proceed with any of the following without first securing all permits required by the North Carolina State Building Code and any other State or local laws applicable to any of the following activities</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: the State Building Code's own permit section (not on disk) requires a permit for this repair.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r49_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r49_in1">
          <text>"deck_resurfacing"</text>
        </inputEntry>
