        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r49_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r49_out1">
          <text>"none"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r49_out2">
          <text>"Over $40,000 the exclusion of 160D-1110(c) does not apply, so 160D-1110(a) requires the permits the State Building Code requires."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(1); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a) (reading): “No permit issued under Article 9 of Chapter 143 of the General Statutes is required for any construction, installation, repair, replacement, or alteration costing forty thousand dollars ($40,000) or less and performed in accordance with the current edition of the North Carolina State Building Code in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building unless the work involves any of the following”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r50">
