        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r51">
        <description>NC: sheds, playhouses, fences, walls, retaining walls, play equipment and storage containers: not settled by statute</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>no person shall commence or proceed with any of the following without first securing all permits required by the North Carolina State Building Code and any other State or local laws applicable to any of the following activities</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: (a) requires only the permits the State Building Code (not on disk) requires.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: whether work on a detached accessory structure is work 'in any single-family residence' is not settled.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(g)" section="160D-1110" subsection="g" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>or to the addition of an accessory building or accessory structure as defined in the North Carolina Residential Code</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: the statute knows accessory buildings as a category (here, for lien agents) but says nothing about exempting small ones from permits.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_in1">
