        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_out0">
          <text>"depends"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_out1">
          <text>"not settled by statute"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r51_out2">
          <text>"The statutes on disk do not settle it: 160D-1110(a) defers to the permits the North Carolina State Building Code requires, which is not on disk, and the $40,000 exclusion reaches work 'in' a single-family residence. Ask the local inspections department. This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a) (reading); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c) (reading); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(g) (reading): “no person shall commence or proceed with any of the following without first securing all permits required by the North Carolina State Building Code and any other State or local laws applicable to any of the following activities”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
