        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r61_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r61_out1">
          <text>"12-A DCMR 105.2 item 12, not available under 105.2.6"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r61_out2">
          <text>"In a Flood Hazard Area, a permit application subject only to review by the Floodplain Administrator is required (and, if historic, ask the Historic Preservation Office as well)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2.6; 12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 12: “and the work is to occur on premises wholly or partially within a Flood Hazard Area, an application for a permit subject only to review by the Floodplain Administrator shall be required.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r62">
        <description>DC: storage container, not in a Flood Hazard Area</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="implied" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Construct, enlarge, alter, repair, move, demolish, raze, or change the occupancy of a building or other structure</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: placing a container on a lot for use as a storage building is erecting a structure under 105.1.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 8" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/8" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>A single garden storage shed that does not exceed 50 square feet (4.65 m2) in area, is less than ten feet (3048 mm) in overall height, is an accessory structure to a building of Use Group R-3 or to a building under the jurisdiction of the Residential Code, and is erected on a lot with no other exempted storage shed.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 17" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/17" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="implied" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Structures erected for a period of less than 180 days in a 12-month period that cover an area of 150 square feet (13.9 m2) or less and are exempted from permit requirements by Section 3103</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: item 17 may reach a container on site for less than 180 days, but it turns on Section 3103, which is model-code text not on disk.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in0">
          <text>"dc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in1">
          <text>"storage_container"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in14">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_out0">
          <text>"depends"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_out1">
          <text>"none named in 12-A DCMR 105.2"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r62_out2">
          <text>"No item of 105.2 names storage containers. A container kept as a storage building is a structure, which 105.1 requires a permit to erect, unless it is a single garden storage shed of 50 sq ft or less (item 8: project 'shed'); a temporary one may fall under item 17, which turns on a model-code section that is not on disk. Ask the code official. This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.1 (reading); 12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 8; 12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 17 (reading): “Construct, enlarge, alter, repair, move, demolish, raze, or change the occupancy of a building or other structure”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r63">
        <description>DC: storage container in a Flood Hazard Area</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2.6" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2.6" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>and the work is to occur on premises wholly or partially within a Flood Hazard Area, an application for a permit subject only to review by the Floodplain Administrator shall be required.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Unless specifically exempted under Section 105.2, an owner or authorized agent who intends to undertake any of the activities set forth in items 1 through 5 below, or to cause any such work to be done shall first make application to the code official and obtain the required permit(s) relevant to the intended work</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>This Section 105.2 sets forth exemptions from permit requirements, subject to historic and Flood Hazard Area restrictions set forth in Sections 105.2.5 and 105.2.6 respectively.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in0">
          <text>"dc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in1">
          <text>"storage_container"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in14">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_out1">
          <text>"any 12-A DCMR 105.2 item, not available under 105.2.6"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r63_out2">
          <text>"An application is required either way: a permit under 105.1 if no item exempts the container, or, if one does, a permit application subject only to review by the Floodplain Administrator (105.2.6)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.2.6; 12-A DCMR 105.1; 12-A DCMR 105.2: “and the work is to occur on premises wholly or partially within a Flood Hazard Area, an application for a permit subject only to review by the Floodplain Administrator shall be required.”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r64">
        <description>DC: farm building</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="implied" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Construct, enlarge, alter, repair, move, demolish, raze, or change the occupancy of a building or other structure</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: no Building item of 105.2 names farm buildings, so erecting one is constructing a structure under 105.1.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.2, Building item 11" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.2/building/11" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Shade cloth structures constructed for horticultural nursery or agricultural purposes, not including service systems.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="12-A DCMR 105.1" section="12-A DCMR 105" subsection="105.1" code="DCMR" jurisdiction="dc" grounding="explicit" url="https://dcregs.dc.gov/Common/DCMR/RuleList.aspx?DownloadFile={64284980-8CFE-4134-BB96-94FBB25965E0}" corpus="regulations" actId="STATE_DC_DCMR_T12_A_C2017_12_A1_S105_EDConstruction_Codes_Supplement_of_2017">
              <lex:quote>Unless specifically exempted under Section 105.2, an owner or authorized agent who intends to undertake any of the activities set forth in items 1 through 5 below, or to cause any such work to be done shall first make application to the code official and obtain the required permit(s) relevant to the intended work</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
