          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_in15">
          <text>true</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_out1">
          <text>"none (trade work)"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r65_out2">
          <text>"105.1 item 2 requires a permit to install, alter, repair or replace any electrical, gas, mechanical or plumbing system, and trade permits are their own class (105.1.1). Ordinary repairs exclude piping, electric wiring and mechanical work (105.2.2), and only the minor items of the Electrical, Gas, Mechanical and Plumbing lists of 105.2 are exempt. Whether the structure itself needs a permit is the answer with trade_work false."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>12-A DCMR 105.1; 12-A DCMR 105.1.1; 12-A DCMR 105.2.2: “Erect, install, enlarge, alter, repair, remove, convert or replace any electrical, gas, mechanical, or plumbing system, the installation of which is regulated by the Construction Codes, or to cause any such work to be done”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r66">
        <description>NC: deck resurfacing, $40,000 or less, two-family dwelling</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(1)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a/1" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The construction, reconstruction, alteration, repair, movement to another site, removal, or demolition of any building or structure.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>no person shall commence or proceed with any of the following without first securing all permits required by the North Carolina State Building Code and any other State or local laws applicable to any of the following activities</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: the State Building Code's own permit section (not on disk) requires a permit for this repair.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in1">
          <text>"deck_resurfacing"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in12">
          <text>&lt;= 40000</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_in16">
          <text>"two_family"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_out0">
          <text>"yes"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_out1">
          <text>"none"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r66_out2">
          <text>"The $40,000 exclusion reaches only work in a single-family residence, farm building or commercial building (160D-1110(c), 143-138(b5)), and a two-family dwelling is none of them. So 160D-1110(a) requires the permits the State Building Code requires; that the Code requires one for this repair is a reading, and it would change if the code books exempt the work."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(1); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a) (reading): “in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r67">
        <description>NC: deck resurfacing, $40,000 or less, townhouse</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: whether a townhouse unit is a 'single-family residence' is not settled by the statutes.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(1)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c/1" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>However, no permit is required for replacement of windows, doors, exterior siding, or the pickets, railings, stair treads, and decking of porches and exterior decks that otherwise meet the requirements of this subsection.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in1">
          <text>"deck_resurfacing"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in5">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in6">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in7">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in12">
          <text>&lt;= 40000</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in15">
          <text>false</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_in16">
          <text>"townhouse"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_out0">
          <text>"depends"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_out1">
          <text>"G.S. 160D-1110(c)(1), if a townhouse unit is a single-family residence"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r67_out2">
          <text>"If a townhouse unit is a 'single-family residence', the $40,000 exclusion applies and no permit is needed; the statutes do not say whether it is. Ask the local inspections department. This is for the structure alone: wiring, plumbing, gas or mechanical work with it needs a permit (trade_work)."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c) (reading); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(1): “in any single-family residence, farm building, or commercial building”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r68">
        <description>NC: farm building</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b4)" section="143-138" subsection="b4" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_143/GS_143-138.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C143_S143-138">
              <lex:quote>Building rules do not apply to (i) farm buildings that are located outside the building-rules jurisdiction of any municipality, (ii) farm buildings that are located inside the building-rules jurisdiction of any municipality if the farm buildings are greenhouses or therapeutic equine facilities</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b4)(1)" section="143-138" subsection="b4/1" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_143/GS_143-138.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C143_S143-138">
              <lex:quote>A "farm building" means any nonresidential building or structure that is used for a bona fide farm purpose as provided in G.S. 160D-903(a).</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in1">
          <text>"farm_building"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in4">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
