          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in8">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in9">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in10">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in11">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in12">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in13">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in14">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in15">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_in16">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_out0">
          <text>"depends"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_out1">
          <text>"G.S. 143-138(b4), if the building qualifies and where it is"</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_permit_required_r68_out2">
          <text>"Building rules do not apply to farm buildings outside any municipality's building-rules jurisdiction, or to greenhouses and therapeutic equine facilities inside one (143-138(b4)). North Carolina's farm building is a nonresidential building or structure used for a bona fide farm purpose. The answer turns on whether this one qualifies and whether it is inside a municipality's building-rules jurisdiction. Ask the county or city inspections department."</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <annotationEntry>
          <text>N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b4); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 143-138(b4)(1): “Building rules do not apply to (i) farm buildings that are located outside the building-rules jurisdiction of any municipality, (ii) farm buildings that are located inside the building-rules jurisdiction of any municipality if the farm buildings are greenhouses or therapeutic equine facilities”</text>
        </annotationEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_permit_required_r69">
        <description>NC: plumbing, heating or cooling, or electrical work</description>
        <extensionElements>
          <lex:grounding>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(2)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a/2" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The installation, extension, or general repair of any plumbing system</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(3)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a/3" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The installation, extension, alteration, or general repair of any heating or cooling equipment system.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)(4)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a/4" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The installation, extension, alteration, or general repair of any electrical wiring, devices, appliances, or equipment</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(2)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c/2" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The addition or change in the design of plumbing.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(c)(3)" section="160D-1110" subsection="c/3" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="explicit" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>The addition, replacement, or change in the design of heating, air-conditioning, or electrical wiring, devices, appliances, or equipment, other than like-kind replacement of electrical devices and lighting fixtures.</lex:quote>
            </lex:source>
            <lex:source citation="N.C. Gen. Stat. § 160D-1110(a)" section="160D-1110" subsection="a" code="N.C. Gen. Stat." jurisdiction="nc" grounding="implied" url="https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-1110.html" corpus="statutes" actId="STATE_NC_C160D_S160D-1110">
              <lex:quote>no person shall commence or proceed with any of the following without first securing all permits required by the North Carolina State Building Code and any other State or local laws applicable to any of the following activities</lex:quote>
              <lex:note>Reading: the State Building Code's own permit sections (not on disk) require permits for this work.</lex:note>
            </lex:source>
          </lex:grounding>
        </extensionElements>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r69_in0">
          <text>"nc"</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_permit_required_r69_in1">
